  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Three ways to say a consonant",
   "texto": [
    "In Korean there are **normales**, **aspiradas** and **tensas** consonants, and they change the meaning.",
    "**aspiradas** () is said to be releasing a **soplo de aire**, such as «k» in English «key». Look, they're the normal ones with one more line.",
    "The **tensas** () are written double and called **secas y fuertes**, without any air. They are very similar to the k, t and p of Spanish said with energy.",
    "In the pronunciation you will see the tensas with double letter: kk, tt, pp, ss, jj."
   ]
